WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:02.068
[music playing]

00:00:02.134 --> 00:00:03.402
 John, Jeff, you
gentlemen are entering

00:00:03.469 --> 00:00:06.138
the final round of this
three-round competition.

00:00:06.205 --> 00:00:07.573
Now we're sending
you back to your home

00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:12.044
forge to recreate this
iconic weapon from history.

00:00:12.111 --> 00:00:19.486
That weapon is the
messer and by-knife.

00:00:22.254 --> 00:00:23.689
 It going to be a challenge.

00:00:23.789 --> 00:00:24.791
 Good luck, bladesmiths.

00:00:24.857 --> 00:00:27.426
We will see you in four days.

00:00:27.493 --> 00:00:28.762
 [inaudible]

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:36.169
 So I'm back at my
home forge, and I'm

00:00:36.269 --> 00:00:37.804
really excited about that.

00:00:37.870 --> 00:00:43.075
But I get four days to make
two blades, and that's insane.

00:00:43.142 --> 00:00:44.977
I don't have time
to do one at a time.

00:00:45.077 --> 00:00:46.946
This is going to be
two irons in the fire

00:00:47.012 --> 00:00:48.982
and swapping them in and out.

00:00:49.049 --> 00:00:50.917
You know, I'd much rather
be able to concentrate

00:00:50.984 --> 00:00:54.621
on one thing, but it's
"Forged in Fire," baby.

00:00:54.687 --> 00:00:56.456
Got the blades all forged out.

00:00:56.522 --> 00:00:58.224
One of the parameters
for the sword

00:00:58.290 --> 00:01:00.460
is that it has to have a fuller.

00:01:00.526 --> 00:01:02.995 line:0%
Putting these fullers
in is probably

00:01:03.062 --> 00:01:04.664 line:7%
the most nerve-racking part.

00:01:04.764 --> 00:01:05.765 line:7%
You can get them too deep.

00:01:05.831 --> 00:01:06.999 line:7%
You can get them off-centered.

00:01:07.066 --> 00:01:08.768 line:0%
Screwing these fullers
up could mean day

00:01:08.834 --> 00:01:11.504 line:7%
one is starting over tomorrow.

00:01:11.571 --> 00:01:13.306
Yes, sir, that'll work.

00:01:15.908 --> 00:01:17.110
 I'm finally home.

00:01:17.176 --> 00:01:18.344
I'm ready to roll.

00:01:18.445 --> 00:01:18.911
Check it once.

00:01:18.978 --> 00:01:19.712
Check it twice.

00:01:19.778 --> 00:01:21.013
Check it 10 times.

00:01:21.080 --> 00:01:22.582
Today, I want to start
with my by-knife,

00:01:22.648 --> 00:01:24.850
so I know how much time
I have to work with

00:01:24.917 --> 00:01:26.352
to make that long messer.

00:01:26.419 --> 00:01:29.188
Blade's got to be
between here and here.

00:01:29.255 --> 00:01:32.424
This homie don't
mess up his lengths.

00:01:32.491 --> 00:01:34.227
I've managed to forge
out the by-knife.

00:01:34.293 --> 00:01:35.562
Things are going a
lot quicker than I

00:01:35.662 --> 00:01:37.063
ever expect they would be.

00:01:37.130 --> 00:01:38.431
I'm liking it.

00:01:38.498 --> 00:01:40.967
So, I'm going to start
attacking the long messer.

00:01:41.033 --> 00:01:43.603
I've never done anything
quite that size.

00:01:43.703 --> 00:01:44.804
Come here, you big monster.

00:01:44.871 --> 00:01:46.406
It's scaring the
bejeebers out of me.

00:01:46.472 --> 00:01:48.073
Still got my fingers
crossed that I've got

00:01:48.173 --> 00:01:51.544
the length I want.

00:01:51.611 --> 00:01:52.645
 I'm ready to quench.

00:01:52.712 --> 00:01:57.517
Two quenches, twice the
work, twice the worry.

00:01:57.617 --> 00:01:58.518
Yes, sir.

00:01:58.618 --> 00:02:00.553
The messer sword is
up to temperature,

00:02:00.620 --> 00:02:03.289
and it's time to quench.

00:02:03.356 --> 00:02:04.523
Here comes the real test.

00:02:04.624 --> 00:02:05.892
Please be hard.

00:02:05.992 --> 00:02:07.794
Yes.

00:02:07.894 --> 00:02:09.595
Hell, yes.

00:02:09.662 --> 00:02:10.562
This is my baby now.

00:02:10.629 --> 00:02:11.364
[laughs]

00:02:11.431 --> 00:02:13.333
So let me take care of it.

00:02:13.433 --> 00:02:16.636
 Today, I need to get
the messer heat treated.

00:02:16.736 --> 00:02:20.240
If it cracks, I don't know that
I'm going to have enough time

00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:21.607
to make another one.

00:02:21.707 --> 00:02:23.809
Well, that's 18 hours
of busting my butt.

00:02:23.876 --> 00:02:25.244
It comes up to this.

00:02:25.344 --> 00:02:28.447
Right now, the only plan
B I can think of is cry.

00:02:28.547 --> 00:02:30.817
[rock music]

00:02:37.723 --> 00:02:39.392
[sighs]

00:02:39.458 --> 00:02:40.760
That's called a sigh of relief.

00:02:43.662 --> 00:02:46.799
[laughs]

00:02:46.865 --> 00:02:49.035
This son of a gun is straight.

00:02:49.135 --> 00:02:50.370
Oh, that worked great.

00:02:53.105 --> 00:02:55.107
 I'm starting day
four, and I'm a lot more

00:02:55.174 --> 00:02:56.843
tired than I was at day one.

00:02:56.909 --> 00:02:59.345
I'm getting the parts
together for the messer sword.

00:02:59.411 --> 00:03:01.480
I'm doing the final
fit and grind on them.

00:03:01.547 --> 00:03:02.415
[laughs]

00:03:02.482 --> 00:03:03.516
Duel weld.

00:03:03.616 --> 00:03:05.751
That thing just makes
you feel like a bad ass

00:03:05.818 --> 00:03:07.052
when you're holding it.

00:03:07.119 --> 00:03:08.620
I mean, I have to chop
something with it.

00:03:08.721 --> 00:03:11.624
So to test my messer
sword, I do an antler chop.

00:03:11.691 --> 00:03:15.461
Antler is some tough stuff,
and if it survives it,

00:03:15.561 --> 00:03:17.363
it should survive anything.

00:03:17.463 --> 00:03:19.265
Hopefully it doesn't break.

00:03:19.365 --> 00:03:20.833
I'm getting what I want.

00:03:20.933 --> 00:03:23.403
I'm still trying to get it a
little sharper for slicing,

00:03:23.503 --> 00:03:27.540
but for chopping, man,
it's freaking awesome.

00:03:27.607 --> 00:03:29.509
 All right,
bladesmiths, this is

00:03:29.575 --> 00:03:31.778
the pig carcass slice and dice.

00:03:31.844 --> 00:03:33.379
I will take your weapon
and deliver killing

00:03:33.446 --> 00:03:35.748
blows on this pig carcass.

00:03:35.848 --> 00:03:36.649
John, you're up first.

00:03:36.749 --> 00:03:37.416
You ready for this?

00:03:37.483 --> 00:03:38.951
 Let's make some bacon, bud.

00:03:39.018 --> 00:03:40.886
This is not an
easy test to pass.

00:03:40.953 --> 00:03:44.090
This is where I find out, did
I make a sword or a couple

00:03:44.190 --> 00:03:46.125
pieces of scrap metal?

00:03:46.192 --> 00:03:49.295
[music playing]

00:03:52.198 --> 00:03:53.233
Oh, yeah.

00:04:03.709 --> 00:04:05.144
Yes.

00:04:05.210 --> 00:04:06.045
 All right, John.

00:04:06.145 --> 00:04:08.347
Your messer is sharp.

00:04:08.414 --> 00:04:12.084
It's a little bit forward-heavy,
but the weight lends

00:04:12.150 --> 00:04:14.386
itself to chop the pig in half.

00:04:14.486 --> 00:04:15.922
Now, your by-knife, razor sharp.

00:04:15.988 --> 00:04:18.424
Those cuts alone were cutting
deeply with every move.

00:04:18.490 --> 00:04:20.559
And overall, sir, it will kill.

00:04:20.626 --> 00:04:22.295
 Oh, yes.

00:04:22.395 --> 00:04:23.496
 All right, Jeff.
Your turn.

00:04:23.563 --> 00:04:24.063
You ready?

00:04:24.163 --> 00:04:24.964
 Yes, sir.

00:04:25.031 --> 00:04:25.965
 Let's do this.

00:04:26.032 --> 00:04:29.535
[music playing]

00:04:41.914 --> 00:04:44.784
[laughter]

00:04:44.850 --> 00:04:45.884
 All right, Jeff.

00:04:45.984 --> 00:04:48.987
Your messer, beautiful balance.

00:04:49.054 --> 00:04:50.156
It's not forward-heavy.

00:04:50.222 --> 00:04:51.624
It actually is
something I can wield.

00:04:51.690 --> 00:04:54.060
Forward, same balance
on the recovery

00:04:54.126 --> 00:04:56.162
when I'm pulling back to cut.

00:04:56.229 --> 00:04:57.663
Now, your by-knife.

00:04:57.763 --> 00:05:01.067
The edge is razor sharp
with every cut and stab

00:05:01.134 --> 00:05:02.334
that it does.

00:05:02.434 --> 00:05:05.271
Overall, sir, your
weapons, they will kill.

00:05:05.338 --> 00:05:06.039
 Thanks, sir.

00:05:09.341 --> 00:05:10.776
 All right, gentlemen.

00:05:10.843 --> 00:05:12.979
Now, to test the strength and
durability of your blades,

00:05:13.046 --> 00:05:14.981
I'll be chopping
into our log here.

00:05:15.081 --> 00:05:17.116
Now remember, this is not
about what your messers are

00:05:17.183 --> 00:05:19.084
going to do that log,
but what that log

00:05:19.151 --> 00:05:20.353
might do to your messers.

00:05:20.419 --> 00:05:21.887
And then I'm going to
take your by-knives,

00:05:21.954 --> 00:05:24.456
and we're going to do a tip
test by driving that tip

00:05:24.556 --> 00:05:26.125
of your blade into that log.

00:05:26.191 --> 00:05:27.693
All right, John you're up.
You ready?

00:05:27.760 --> 00:05:28.428
 Do your worst.

00:05:28.528 --> 00:05:29.228
 OK.

00:05:29.295 --> 00:05:32.799
[music playing]

00:05:55.588 --> 00:05:58.324
All right, John, well, let's
start with your messer.

00:05:58.391 --> 00:06:01.060
Your edge is still sharp.

00:06:01.126 --> 00:06:02.661
Blade's still straight and true.

00:06:02.728 --> 00:06:04.630
Your blade's got a
lot of weight to it.

00:06:04.697 --> 00:06:07.399
Your handle is a
little confusing

00:06:07.466 --> 00:06:08.967
when you're swinging this.

00:06:09.067 --> 00:06:11.036
Having that bead right there,
my hand kind of wants to go

00:06:11.103 --> 00:06:12.404
all the way up to the guard.

00:06:12.471 --> 00:06:15.708
And having this, the
well, further back sort of

00:06:15.775 --> 00:06:19.212
pushes my hand a little bit back
behind where I'd like it to be.

00:06:19.312 --> 00:06:22.148
As far as your by-knife
goes, not a mark on it.

00:06:22.214 --> 00:06:23.082
Really well done.

00:06:23.149 --> 00:06:24.116
 Thank you, sir.

00:06:24.216 --> 00:06:25.350
 All right, Jeff.

00:06:25.450 --> 00:06:26.285
Your turn.
You ready?

00:06:26.352 --> 00:06:27.052
 Yes, sir.

00:06:27.119 --> 00:06:27.887
 OK.

00:06:27.954 --> 00:06:31.391
[music playing]

00:06:52.811 --> 00:06:54.613
All right, let's start
with your messer.

00:06:54.680 --> 00:06:56.682
What I really like
about this blade

00:06:56.782 --> 00:06:58.384
is the way you balanced it.

00:06:58.484 --> 00:07:00.686
It puts all that weight
right back in my hand

00:07:00.787 --> 00:07:01.754
where I want it.

00:07:01.854 --> 00:07:03.623
Your knife, it's a
really pretty piece.

00:07:03.723 --> 00:07:06.491
It's very comfortable
in the hand, but just

00:07:06.558 --> 00:07:08.361
a little brittle on the tip.

00:07:08.427 --> 00:07:10.329
But they are both
beautiful pieces.

00:07:10.429 --> 00:07:11.263
Nicely done.

00:07:11.330 --> 00:07:12.031
 Thanks, sir.

00:07:14.367 --> 00:07:18.237
 All right, bladesmiths,
the rope slice surprise.

00:07:18.337 --> 00:07:19.771
Now, unlike the
strength test, this

00:07:19.871 --> 00:07:22.240
is all about what your edge will
do to different materials we

00:07:22.341 --> 00:07:23.876
have out here.

00:07:23.943 --> 00:07:24.510
John, you're up first.

00:07:24.577 --> 00:07:25.411
You ready for this?

00:07:25.478 --> 00:07:26.244
 Please do, sir.

00:07:26.345 --> 00:07:26.979
 Let's do this.

00:07:31.350 --> 00:07:35.221
[music playing]

00:07:43.496 --> 00:07:45.064
All right, John.

00:07:45.131 --> 00:07:46.532
During the first couple, your
by-knife, it's a light knife.

00:07:46.599 --> 00:07:47.566
It didn't cut all
the way through.

00:07:47.633 --> 00:07:48.967
It started to unravel.

00:07:49.034 --> 00:07:51.036
And of course, your
messer finished that off.

00:07:51.103 --> 00:07:55.741
On these tubes, this cut
cleanly all the way through.

00:07:55.841 --> 00:07:58.711
Your weapons, sir, will cut.

00:07:58.811 --> 00:07:59.644
 Thank you.

00:07:59.745 --> 00:08:00.879
 All right, Jeff.
It's your turn.

00:08:00.980 --> 00:08:01.447
You ready, sir?

00:08:01.514 --> 00:08:03.281
 Yes, sir.

00:08:03.382 --> 00:08:07.854
[music playing]

00:08:16.595 --> 00:08:17.462
 All right, Jeff.

00:08:17.529 --> 00:08:19.631
First up your by-knife.

00:08:19.698 --> 00:08:22.601
Despite the fact that
just the tip broke off,

00:08:22.668 --> 00:08:23.935
the edge is razor sharp.

00:08:24.002 --> 00:08:26.706
With one cut, it cut
cleanly through the rope.

00:08:26.772 --> 00:08:29.341
Your messer, once
again, the balance

00:08:29.407 --> 00:08:30.575
just feels so good in the hand.

00:08:30.675 --> 00:08:34.914
It's such an easy weapon
to wield and slice.

00:08:34.980 --> 00:08:38.049
Overall, sir, your
weapons will cut.

00:08:38.150 --> 00:08:39.251
 Thank you, sir.

00:08:39.318 --> 00:08:40.286
 They're going
to be judging both

00:08:40.352 --> 00:08:41.887
of these weapons, not just one.

00:08:41.953 --> 00:08:45.758
The knife broke, but the sword
performed above and beyond.

00:08:45.824 --> 00:08:46.993
It's anybody's game, I think.

00:08:50.329 --> 00:08:54.200
 Bladesmiths, the judges'
deliberation is complete.

00:08:54.267 --> 00:08:56.969
They've made their
final decision.

00:08:57.069 --> 00:09:03.208
Our new "Forged in
Fire" Champion is Jeff.

00:09:03.309 --> 00:09:04.443
Congratulations.

00:09:04.543 --> 00:09:05.978
You're the new "Forged
in Fire" Champion.

00:09:06.045 --> 00:09:09.348
John, unfortunately, your
blades did not make the cut.

00:09:09.415 --> 00:09:12.285
 John, while Jeff's
by-knife's tip broke

00:09:12.351 --> 00:09:14.053
on the strength
test, it outperformed

00:09:14.153 --> 00:09:15.754
yours on the sharpness test.

00:09:15.854 --> 00:09:18.424
The combination of the
balance, the forward weight,

00:09:18.491 --> 00:09:20.392
and your handle design,
well, that's the reason

00:09:20.459 --> 00:09:21.894
we're sending you home.

00:09:21.960 --> 00:09:23.996
 John, please
surrender your blades.

00:09:24.063 --> 00:09:25.364
[music playing]

00:09:25.464 --> 00:09:26.531
 Somebody has to win.

00:09:26.598 --> 00:09:28.234
And I wish it
could have been me.

00:09:28.300 --> 00:09:30.902
But I honestly feel the judges
made the right decision.

00:09:30.969 --> 00:09:35.641
Jeff's messer was a work of
art, and he deserved to win.

00:09:35.708 --> 00:09:38.009
What I loved about
this is that it

00:09:38.110 --> 00:09:40.846
stretched me far beyond
what I thought I could do,

00:09:40.947 --> 00:09:41.681
and I did it.

00:09:45.217 --> 00:09:46.585
 Jeff, congratulations.

00:09:46.652 --> 00:09:48.120
You're the new "Forged
in Fire" Champion.

00:09:48.187 --> 00:09:50.756
And that's a title that comes
with a check for $10,000.

00:09:50.823 --> 00:09:52.157
How do you feel right now?

00:09:52.224 --> 00:09:54.092
 [laughs]

00:09:54.159 --> 00:09:55.227
Validated.

00:09:55.328 --> 00:09:59.264
 Sir, please, present
your blades to the judges.

00:09:59.331 --> 00:10:00.933
 I'm happy.

00:10:01.033 --> 00:10:03.402
I can't even describe
my emotions right now.

00:10:03.469 --> 00:10:06.905
"Forged in Fire" Champion, baby,
bringing it back to Kentucky.

00:10:06.972 --> 00:10:08.841
Hell yeah!

00:10:08.941 --> 00:10:09.407
Yes!

00:10:09.508 --> 00:10:12.612
[music playing]

